The messaging gateway makes outbound connections. It does not need an
inbound pf rule for Telegram, Discord, Slack, or the other polling adapters.

The dashboard is separate. If you start it with --host 0.0.0.0, inbound TCP
9119 must be allowed. An example ruleset, based on /etc/examples/pf.conf,
is installed at

	${PREFIX}/share/examples/hermes-agent/pf.conf

This package does not replace /etc/pf.conf. Merge that example yourself,
check it with `pfctl -nf`, then load it with `pfctl -f`. A hosting provider
firewall can still drop 9119 after pf allows it.
